<h1>Medicaid Provider Fraud Intelligence System (EBV Detector)</h1>
<h2>Model Architecture & Machine Learning Specification Document</h2>
<p><strong>Document ID:</strong> <code>DOC-EBV-ML-SPEC-001</code>  </p>
<p><strong>Classification:</strong> State Medicaid Program Integrity / Law Enforcement Sensitive  </p>
<p><strong>Target Threat:</strong> "Enroll, Bill, Vanish" (EBV) Sham Healthcare Provider Syndicates  </p>
<p><strong>Compliance Standards:</strong> 42 CFR Part 455, NC RFP Attachment C §3, ADR-0001 Architecture  </p>
<p><strong>Release Version:</strong> <code>1.0.0-PROD</code>  </p>
<hr>
<h3>Executive Summary</h3>
<p>Medicaid "Enroll, Bill, Vanish" (EBV) fraud occurs when organized criminal rings establish shell provider organizations, disguise beneficial ownership, rapidly bill millions of dollars in fabricated healthcare claims, and vanish before traditional 12-to-18-month post-payment audits discover the scheme.</p>
<p>This system shifts fraud prevention from retrospective "pay-and-chase" audits to real-time pre-payment intervention across two checkpoints:</p>
<p>1. <strong>Checkpoint 1 (Pre-Enrollment Screening):</strong> Evaluates provider applications in real time using probabilistic entity resolution, physical address hygiene, recursive multi-hop relational graph traversal, and document plagiarism detection.</p>
<p>2. <strong>Checkpoint 2 (Rapid Post-Enrollment Claims Surveillance):</strong> Monitors the first 30 to 90 days of claims billing for impossible physical edits, robust statistical velocity spikes, and bipartite patient cohort recycling.</p>
<p>To comply with federal due process (<strong>42 CFR §455</strong>) and state contract constraints (<strong>NC RFP Attachment C §3</strong>), the architecture strictly adheres to <strong>Architectural Decision Record 0001 (ADR-0001)</strong>:</p>
<p>- <strong>Layer 1 (Authoritative Deterministic Gate):</strong> Deterministic rules evaluating statutory exclusion grounds (§455.416) and physical address bans.</p>
<p>- <strong>Layer 2 (Assistive Advisory Scorer):</strong> Seven specialized machine learning and statistical models that compute an explainable <strong>Advisory Priority Score (0–100)</strong> and recommend <strong>ACA Risk Tiers (§455.450)</strong> while preserving human adjudicative authority.</p>
<hr>
<h3>Model Architecture Overview</h3>
<pre><code>                      Incoming Provider Disclosure / Claims Stream
                                           │
                                           ▼
                       [ Feature Normalization &amp; Ingestion ]
                                           │
     ┌─────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┐
     ▼                                                                           ▼
Checkpoint 1: Pre-Enrollment                                     Checkpoint 2: Post-Enrollment (Days 1–90)
     │                                                                           │
     ├─► Model 1: Fellegi-Sunter Probabilistic Linkage                           ├─► Model 4: Robust MAD Z-Score Outlier
     ├─► Model 2: Spatial Density Clustering &amp; CMRA                              ├─► Hard Physical Edits (&gt;24h, Inpatient)
     ├─► Model 3: Personalized PageRank &amp; Multi-Hop Traversal                    └─► Model 5: Bipartite Patient Migration
     └─► Model 4: MinHash 128-Permutation LSH Document NLP                       │
     │                                                                           │
     ▼                                                                           ▼
Layer 1 Authoritative Rules Gate                                    42 CFR §455.23 Payment Suspension
     │                                                                           │
     ▼                                                                           ▼
Layer 2 Calibrated Advisory Scorer (0-100) ─────────────────────────► WORM Cryptographic SHA-256 Audit
     │
     ▼
Human Investigator Adjudication (HITL)</code></pre>
